                <pb facs="0188" n="76" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg76"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 21158/4.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Kerens to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-09-22"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 22, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 105.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 66 of July 30,
                    1910, transmitting the sworn statement and passport application of Mr. Rudolf
                    Warren-Lippit, may I inquire if the department has reached a decision in the
                    matter, and, if so, the result of same?</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. C. Kerens.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
